{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "102", "sample_idx": 7, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "\"Oh, darling, you look… comfortable,\" Seraphina said, adjusting the delicate lace of her emerald green ball gown. Her voice was a melodic chime.\n\nAcross from her, Leo shrugged, pulling his sweatshirt tighter. \"And you look like you're about to float away. Seriously, Seraphina, is this *really* necessary? It's just the monthly astronomy club meeting.\"\n\nSeraphina gasped dramatically. \"Leo! It's a *celebration* of the cosmos! And Professor Eldridge is presenting his new theories on nebula formation. It requires… ambiance.\" She gestured grandly around the room, which was, admittedly, a slightly cluttered community hall.\n\nLeo chuckled. \"Ambiance? It's got folding chairs and a projector. I brought extra blankets, just in case.\"\n\n\"Blankets? Leo, this is an occasion! Besides,\" she lowered her voice conspiratorially, \"Professor Eldridge *loves* when I make an entrance.\"\n\n\"He also loves accurate data and not being distracted by shimmering gowns,\" Leo countered, but a smile played on his lips. \"Look, I'm just saying, you're going to be freezing in that thing.\"\n\nSeraphina smoothed her skirt. \"Nonsense. I have thermal lining. And think of the photographs! It'll be *divine*.\"\n\n* He sighed, knowing arguing was futile. \"Alright, alright. Just try not to trip over your train.\"\n* \"No promises,\" Seraphina winked, already halfway to the door. \"I’m going to find a telescope before anyone else does.\"\n* \"Just...be careful,\" Leo called after her, watching her disappear into the night. He pulled his hood up and headed in the opposite direction, grabbing the extra blankets.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.06885108351707458}, {"token": "Oh", "logprob": -0.26135382056236267}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.19545312225818634}, {"token": "▁darling", "logprob": -0.04958963766694069}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.079183734953403